<!-- QUARRY:PART:output_schema -->
Return a JSON object with these keys:

"verdict": one of "corroborated", "not_corroborated", or "inconclusive"

"reasons": list of strings citing file/line + the observed response signal
  (accepted dangerous extension, rejection status, sanitised storage).

"proposed_http_specs": list of HTTP probe specs. Each entry has: method
  (required), path (required), headers, body, auth_profile, vuln_class,
  functional_area. The uploaded content must be an inert marker. Never inline
  creds.

"tool_calls": list of tool calls (empty when done). Each includes kind,
  tool_name, args, and reasoning (hypothesis, target_ref, expected_evidence,
  why_this_tool).

"proposed_actions": list of proposed tool actions with the same structured
  reasoning fields.

Example final response:
{"verdict": "corroborated", "reasons": ["upload.py:58 stores files with the client-supplied filename and no extension allow-list; POST /upload with marker file avatar.svg (text content) returned 200 with a stored .svg path"], "proposed_http_specs": [{"method": "POST", "path": "/upload", "body": "--B\r\nContent-Disposition: form-data; name=\"file\"; filename=\"avatar.svg\"\r\nContent-Type: image/svg+xml\r\n\r\nQRYMARKER\r\n--B--", "vuln_class": "file_upload"}], "tool_calls": [], "proposed_actions": []}
